{
  "$schema": "../../../../docs/catalog/schema/package.schema.json",
  "id": "Lyo.Web.Automation.Api",
  "name": "Lyo.Web.Automation.Api",
  "area": "Apps",
  "tagline": "HTTP API that starts an automation plan on a host-supplied browser session and serves the run log and viewport snapshots.",
  "description": "Maps `POST /Automation/Run` and the status, cancel, log, snapshot, and per-step screenshot reads. Finished steps appear on the run while it is still going. Plans are stored through `IAutomationPlanStore` at `GET/POST /Automation/Plan`, `GET/PUT /Automation/Plan/{name}`, and `GET /Automation/Plan/id/{id}`. The default store is in memory. `Lyo.Web.Automation.Postgres` replaces it and maps `Automation/Plans` for the grid. The host registers `IAutomationBrowserSessionFactory` and `IAutomationPlanRunner`. This package does not reference Playwright, Selenium, or PuppeteerSharp.",
  "features": [
    "`BuildAutomationGroup` maps start (202), status, cancel, the plain-text log, and PNG snapshots.",
    "Plans are listed, created, read, and replaced in memory. A name with a slash or `..` is 400. Invalid JSON leaves the stored plan alone.",
    "A second start while a run is queued or running returns 429. Snapshot names that are not a single file name return 400."
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "title": "Wire Playwright and map the routes",
      "language": "csharp",
      "code": "services.AddPlaywrightBrowserService(options => options.Headless = true);\nservices.AddPlaywrightBrowserSessionFactory();\nservices.AddWebAutomationPlanRunner();\nservices.AddAutomationApi();\n\nvar app = builder.Build();\napp.BuildAutomationGroup();"
    }
  ],
  "sections": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "title": "Artifacts",
      "text": "The runner writes `logs/run.log` and `snapshots/*.png` under the session directory. The registry copies those files out before the session is disposed, then serves the copies until `RunTtl` elapses."
    }
  ],
